{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.KazhdanLusztigClassicalLimit","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.KazhdanLusztigClassicalLimit","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.Basic","lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.HeckeAnyonicSubstrate","lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.CrystalGraphRealization"],"declarations":9,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.KazhdanLusztigClassicalLimit.canonical","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.KazhdanLusztigClassicalLimit.canonical","kind":"def","line":129,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/KazhdanLusztigClassicalLimit.lean#L129-L175","doc":"**The trivial model — a `def`, not an `instance`, and not \"faithful\".**\n\nIts docstring said *\"Faithful instance. Carries the explicit research-grade\nconjecture as a sorry.\"* Neither half was true. There is no `sorry`: it sets\n`KLBasisElt := PUnit` and `statSign _ := 1`, so `kl_compatible_with_tau` is\ndischarged by `Or.inl rfl` on `1 = 1`. Every classical limit is bosonic\nbecause there is one basis element and it was declared bosonic. A `sorry`\nwould at least be visible to `#print axioms`; this was not.\n\nAs an unconditional `instance` it made `statSign_klMap_pm_one` and\n`statSign_sq_eq_one` unconditional theorems about a one-element KL basis.\n\n**The class was defective too, and has been repaired.** As written,\n`kl_compatible_with_tau` was `∀ T, statSign (klMap T) = 1 ∨ … = -1` beside a\nsibling field `statSign_pm_one : ∀ b, statSign b = 1 ∨ statSign b = -1`. The\nconjecture was therefore `statSign_pm_one (klMap T)` — derivable in *every*\ninstance, degenerate or not, so the class asserted nothing even given real\ndata. Verified by substitution: both downstream theorems compile unchanged\nwith the sibling in place of the conjectural field.\n\nThe cause was the typing. `statSign` landed in `ℤ`, and `statSign_pm_one`\nthen *axiomatised* the very collapse the conjecture claims to establish —\n\"only ±1\" was true by fiat, leaving no room for an anyonic phase to fail to\ncollapse. `statSign` now lands in the ground ring `R`, where a root of unity\ncan live, `statSign_pm_one` is gone (it was the conjecture wearing an\naxiom's clothes), and `kl_compatible_with_tau` is guarded by `q = 1`. It now\nsays something that can fail: at the classical point the phase is `±1`,\nand away from it nothing is claimed.\n\nStill not stated by any field, and still owed: that the `q → 1` limit of the\nKLR canonical basis *is* the Kazhdan–Lusztig basis, and that the limit\nfunctor is monoidal. Those need `τ` and the KL basis as independent data;\nthis repair makes the statistics field honest, not the whole conjecture.\n\nDemoted the same way as `ConfinementGradingCorrespondence.canonical`\n(bean `qou-fngs`). Nothing consumed it: the class has no users outside this\nfile. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.KazhdanLusztigClassicalLimit.statSign_sq_eq_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.KazhdanLusztigClassicalLimit.statSign_sq_eq_one","kind":"theorem","line":111,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/KazhdanLusztigClassicalLimit.lean#L111-L127","doc":"**Conditional theorem (squared statistic is `+1`).**\n\nConditional on `[KazhdanLusztigClassicalLimit R q]`: the squared\nstatistical sign of any classical-limit image is `+1` — i.e. the\nclassical limit yields ℤ/2-statistics (bosons/fermions only),\nnever higher-order anyonic phases. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.KazhdanLusztigClassicalLimit.statSign_klMap_pm_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.KazhdanLusztigClassicalLimit.statSign_klMap_pm_one","kind":"theorem","line":98,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/KazhdanLusztigClassicalLimit.lean#L98-L109","doc":"Unconditional consequence: every normal form's classical-limit\nstatistic is bosonic or fermionic — no exotic statistics survive\nthe `q → 1` collapse. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.KazhdanLusztigClassicalLimit.kl_compatible_with_tau","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.KazhdanLusztigClassicalLimit.kl_compatible_with_tau","kind":"theorem","line":93,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/KazhdanLusztigClassicalLimit.lean#L93-L93","doc":"**The conjecture itself**: at the classical point `q = 1` the phase\ncollapses to `±1` — Bose/Fermi only, no anyonic phase survives the\nlimit. Plays the role of `sorry`.\n\nThe `q = 1` hypothesis is load-bearing. Without it the field asserts the\ncollapse at every `q`, including the generic anyonic ones where it is\nfalse, so it could only ever be discharged by a degenerate `statSign`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.KazhdanLusztigClassicalLimit.statSign","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.KazhdanLusztigClassicalLimit.statSign","kind":"def","line":85,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/KazhdanLusztigClassicalLimit.lean#L85-L85","doc":"Statistical phase carried by a KL basis element under the observation\nfunctor `τ` (bosonic = `+1`, fermionic = `-1`).\n\nValued in the **ground ring**, not in `ℤ`. The substrate this sits over\nis anyonic (`HeckeAnyonicSubstrate`), so the phase is generically a root\nof unity in `R`; typing it as `ℤ` and asserting `= ±1` made the\nconjecture true by construction, which is exactly what went wrong below. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.KazhdanLusztigClassicalLimit.klMap","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.KazhdanLusztigClassicalLimit.klMap","kind":"def","line":77,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/KazhdanLusztigClassicalLimit.lean#L77-L77","doc":"The `q → 1` classical-limit map `b_w ↦ C_w`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.KazhdanLusztigClassicalLimit.KLBasisElt","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.KazhdanLusztigClassicalLimit.KLBasisElt","kind":"def","line":75,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/KazhdanLusztigClassicalLimit.lean#L75-L75","doc":"Abstract type of Kazhdan–Lusztig basis elements `C_w ∈ ℤ[S_n]`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.KazhdanLusztigClassicalLimit.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.KazhdanLusztigClassicalLimit.mk","kind":"ctor","line":71,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/KazhdanLusztigClassicalLimit.lean#L71-L71","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.KazhdanLusztigClassicalLimit","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.KazhdanLusztigClassicalLimit","kind":"class","line":59,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/KazhdanLusztigClassicalLimit.lean#L59-L94","doc":"**Kazhdan–Lusztig classical limit (conjecture).**\n\nEncodes the `q → 1` specialisation of the KLR canonical basis to\nthe Kazhdan–Lusztig basis of `ℤ[S_n]`, and the compatibility of\nthis limit with the observation functor `τ`.  The\n`kl_compatible_with_tau` field is the conjectural input. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:conj:kazhdan-lusztig-classical-limit","label":"conj:kazhdan-lusztig-classical-limit","md":"quantum-observable-universe/nuclear-interactions/kazhdan-lusztig-classical-limit.md"}],"signatureChunk":0}]}